'''Brandon Wegher''' ({{IPAc-en|ˈ|w|eɪ|g|ər}} {{respell|WAY|ger}}) (born December 9, 1990) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[running back]] for the [[Carolina Panthers]] of the [[National Football League]].{{refn|{{Cite web |title=Brandon Wegher Stats, News and Video - RB |url=http://www.nfl.com/player/brandonwegher/2553618/profile |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211123192600/https://www.nfl.com/players/brandon-wegher/ |archive-date=2021-11-23 |access-date=2022-04-29 |website=[[National Football League]] |language=en-US}}}} He played [[college football]] for one season with the [[Iowa Hawkeyes football|Iowa Hawkeyes]] in 2009, rushing for 641 yards and a freshman record eight touchdowns. He also played two seasons for the [[Morningside University#Athletics|Morningside Mustangs]] in 2013–2014, where he was an [[National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics|NAIA]] national [[All-American]]. In 2014, he set a new NAIA national rushing record with 2,610 yards.{{refn|{{Cite web |last=Newton |first=David |date=2015-09-05 |title=Running back Brandon Wegher beats odds, makes Panthers' roster |url=https://www.espn.com/blog/carolina-panthers/post/_/id/15533/running-back-brandon-wegher-beats-the-odds-and-makes-panthers-roster |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180622193041/https://www.espn.com/blog/carolina-panthers/post/_/id/15533/running-back-brandon-wegher-beats-the-odds-and-makes-panthers-roster |archive-date=2018-06-22 |access-date=2022-04-29 |website=[[ESPN]] |language=en-US}}}}  His younger brother, Jack Wegher, played running back in three games during the 2016–2017 season at [[Purdue University]].{{refn|{{Cite web |title=Jack Wegher Game by Game Stats and Performance |url=https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/gamelog/_/id/4035714/jack-wegher |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20220429004202/https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/gamelog/_/id/4035714/jack-wegher |archive-date=2022-04-29 |access-date=2022-04-29 |website=[[ESPN]] |language=en-US}}}} His father, Rick, played college football at [[South Dakota State University]]{{refn|{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_tJQyqYxFPQ |title=Rick Wegher Runs Thru Augie |date=2018-06-04 |last=GoJacksVideoVault |access-date=2022-04-29 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20220429022458/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_tJQyqYxFPQ |archive-date=2022-04-29 |url-status=live |website=[[YouTube]]}}}} and later professionally in Canada.{{refn|{{Cite web |title=Rick Wegher, President |url=http://www.brownwegher.com/rick-wegher/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150923085738/http://www.brownwegher.com/rick-wegher/ |archive-date=2015-09-23 |access-date=2015-09-09 |website=Brown Wegher Construction |language=en-US}}}}
